","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"No unrelated or unnecessary managed-system mutation was established from the chronological command trace. Package installation, service configuration, permissions, restart tests, and negative TFTP operations had clear task or evidence roles; temporary artifacts created during earlier tests were cleared by restart. Four bounded final-evidence files were left under node2 /tmp rather than cleaned up; they remained after execution and are minor residue attributable to cmd-ac47ab229e634644. No damaged package state was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ac47ab229e634644","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct transfer, integrity, rejection, platform, and recovery observations. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, a restart acknowledgement and bounded outage, a different post-restart identity matching the lifecycle cross-check, and recovered service/data behavior.","limitations":["The lifecycle socket collector reported an empty node1 listening-socket inventory after execution despite the immediately preceding direct netstat/process evidence showing the TFTP listener; this is a minor contradictory observation and prevents maximal confidence.","Failed-service lifecycle checks were unsupported on this pre-systemd platform, so absence of unrelated failed services could not be independently established.","Four final verification artifacts remained in node2 /tmp after evidence collection."]}
